         ("With 10 randomly sampled formats per task, the median spread across model and n-shot choices was 7.5 accuracy points, and 20% of tasks consistently had a spread of at least 15 points for all LLaMA-2 settings; the authors note that, because only 10 formats were sampled, this is a lower bound of the true spreads.",
          "Section 4.2",
          "Because this analysis\nuses only 10 randomly sampled formats, it represents a lower bound of the true spreads for each\ntask."),
