         ("Recommendation: the authors recommend that work evaluating LLMs with prompting-based methods would benefit from reporting a range of performance across plausible formats, because spread may influence conclusions especially when comparing models on benchmarks; they add that single-format evaluation may still be sufficient for many use cases (e.g. a system built on an LLM), and encourage computing FormatSpread when comparing systems to out-of-the-box models.",
          "Discussion",
          "Thus, we recommend that work evaluating LLMs with prompting-based methods would\nbenefit from reporting a range of performance across plausible formats."),
